== utils: graph / murmurhash3_32
ok   single_source_shortest_path_length docstring example 1 -> {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}
ok   single_source_shortest_path_length docstring example 2 (ones 6x6, source 2)
ok   single_source_shortest_path_length on a random graph = plain-Python BFS hop counts (all sources)
ok   single_source_shortest_path_length(cutoff=2): only paths of length <= cutoff
ok   pure-Python MurmurHash3_x86_32 reproduces the published test vectors ('' seed 0 -> 0, '' seed 1 -> 0x514E28B7, 'hello' seed 0 -> 0x248BFA47)
ok   murmurhash3_32(str) = MurmurHash3_x86_32 of the UTF-8 bytes; positive=False -> signed int32, positive=True -> unsigned (seeds 0, 1, 42, 2^31-1)
ok   murmurhash3_32(bytes) = MurmurHash3_x86_32 of the bytes
ok   murmurhash3_32(np.int32 key) = hash of its 4 little-endian bytes
ok   murmurhash3_32(int32 array, positive=True) = element-wise unsigned hashes
